---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StrategyClusters from '../../../components/strategy-connect/StrategyClusters.astro';
import ArticleSection from '../../../components/content/article/ArticleSection.astro';
import ArticleTwoCol from '../../../components/content/article/ArticleTwoCol.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../../components/ui/SectionLabel.astro';
import NavRow from '../../../components/ui/NavRow.astro';
import KeepExploring from '../../../components/content/KeepExploring.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Strategy Connect / Engage+ — A different way to listen" description="An AI-powered conversation for each participant, with tools to help organisations understand what emerges across them." image="/media/work/cluster.png" current="shipped">
  <article class="strategy-story">
    <header class="container strategy-hero"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label" withDot>Shipped / Strategy + AI</SectionLabel>
      <h1>How do you have a meaningful conversation with 1,000 people?</h1>
      <p class="lede">Organisations spend a lot of time trying to understand what their people think.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Surveys can reach everyone, but often limit what people can say. Conversations give people room to explain themselves, but they're difficult to conduct at scale.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Engage+ brings those two things together.</strong></p>
      <p class="body-copy">An AI-powered conversation for each participant, with tools to help organisations understand what emerges across them.</p>
      <div class="strategy-meta"><span>Strategy Connect / Engage+</span><span>Paul Kerr × Aidan Nuttall / Strategy Connect</span><span>Conversational AI · Semantic analysis · Product architecture</span></div>
    </ArticleTwoCol></header>

    <ArticleSection dark id="the-problem"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">01 / The problem</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Listening to everyone is harder than asking everyone.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Strategy Connect has spent years helping organisations develop and manage strategy.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Aidan Nuttall and his team work with organisations to understand where they are, where they want to go and how to get there.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">An important part of that work is listening.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Leadership teams have workshops. Stakeholders are interviewed. Employees complete surveys.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">But there is a trade-off.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Surveys give you scale. Conversations give you depth.</strong></p>
      <p class="body-copy">We wanted to find out whether AI could help us have both.</p>

    </ArticleTwoCol>

    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="engage"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">02 / The conversation</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">What if everyone could have their say?</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Engage+ gives participants a familiar conversational interface.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">The AI asks a question, listens to the response and can follow up when there's something worth exploring.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">People can explain what they think in their own words rather than choosing from a predefined list of answers.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">One conversation might be short. Another might uncover something nobody thought to ask about.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>The conversation follows the person, not just the questionnaire.</strong></p>
<figure class="phone"><img src="/media/work/clusterphone.png" alt="Engage+ mobile conversation about AI development and human oversight" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Engage+ / A participant having a conversation with the AI.</figcaption></figure>
    </ArticleTwoCol>

    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="perspectives"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">03 / The next problem</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">A thousand conversations create a thousand perspectives.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Having the conversations is only the first challenge.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Now imagine hundreds or thousands of people have participated.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">You've collected a substantial amount of information, but understanding it is another problem entirely.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">What are people agreeing on?</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Where do their views differ?</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Which ideas keep appearing?</p>
      <p class="body-copy">What are the unusual perspectives that might otherwise be missed?</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Collecting the conversations isn't enough. You need to understand them.</strong></p>

    </ArticleTwoCol>

    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="signal"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">04 / Finding the patterns</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Making sense of what people are saying.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Engage+ uses semantic analysis to explore relationships between responses.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Contributions with similar meanings can be grouped into clusters, making it easier to identify common themes and different perspectives.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">The visualisation lets people explore those relationships and return to the underlying contributions.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">It's a way to move between the bigger picture and the individual voices that created it.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>The patterns matter. So do the people behind them.</strong></p>

    </ArticleTwoCol>
      <figure class="wide"><StrategyClusters dataSrc="/media/strategy-connect/demo-data.json" /><figcaption>Engage+ / Exploring relationships between conversations and the ideas within them. Interactive demonstration using 720 synthetic responses; this is not participant data or the original analysis.</figcaption></figure>
    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="real-people"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">05 / The real world</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Real conversations don't follow a script.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">One of the biggest lessons came when Engage+ was used with real participants.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">An unexpected, serious response required escalation.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">It was a reminder that a conversational interface creates responsibilities that a conventional survey doesn't necessarily have in the same way.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">People can say anything.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">They can raise sensitive issues, misunderstand a question, go off-topic or disclose something that needs attention.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">That means thinking carefully about how the system handles unexpected responses, when it should stop, and when a person needs to become involved.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>The conversation might be powered by AI. The responsibility doesn't disappear.</strong></p>

    </ArticleTwoCol>

    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="together"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">06 / The bigger opportunity</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">What if strategy could hear from the whole organisation?</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Traditional strategy development often begins with leadership teams, workshops and selected stakeholders.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Engage+ creates the possibility of including a much broader range of perspectives.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Not to replace the people responsible for developing strategy, but to give them a better understanding of the organisation they're making decisions for.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">That's where Engage+ and Strategy Connect begin to connect.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">The original platform helps organisations develop and manage strategy.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Engage+ helps them listen more broadly.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Aidan is exploring how those capabilities might come together.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Better strategy starts with understanding the people it affects.</strong></p>

    </ArticleTwoCol>

    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="what-we-built"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">07 / What we built</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">A different way to listen.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Engage+ began with a question about whether AI could make meaningful conversations possible at a scale that would otherwise be difficult.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">The result brings together conversational AI, semantic analysis and interactive visualisation.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">The interesting part isn't any one of those technologies.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">It's what they make possible together.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Give people room to speak.</strong></p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Find the patterns across what they say.</strong></p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Keep the individual voices visible.</strong></p>
      <p class="body-copy">That's the product we're continuing to explore.</p>

    </ArticleTwoCol>

    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="the-people"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">The people behind it</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">The people behind it</h2>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Aidan Nuttall / Strategy Connect</strong><br />Product vision, strategy expertise and domain knowledge.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Paul Kerr / Product Architecture</strong><br />Technical architecture and development.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol><figure class="wide interview">
        <div class="video-frame"><iframe id="aidan-interview" title="Aidan Nuttall on scaling meaningful conversations with AI" data-video-id="11dftwJtcgM" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/11dftwJtcgM?enablejsapi=1&amp;playsinline=1&amp;rel=0" loading="lazy" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"></iframe></div>
        <figcaption>Aidan Nuttall / Scaling meaningful conversations with AI. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=11dftwJtcgM" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch on YouTube ↗</a></figcaption>
      </figure></ArticleSection>
    <ArticleSection dark id="related-learning"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">Related Learning</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">A New Way to Build Software</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">The separate story of how AI-assisted development changed the economics of rebuilding the original Strategy Connect platform.</p>
      <NavRow href="/learnings/the-moment-software-development-changed/" label="Read the learning" description="A New Way to Build Software →" />
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>
  </article>
  <KeepExploring routes={['learnings', 'building', 'shipped']} />
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  interface VideoPlayer { mute(): void; playVideo(): void; pauseVideo(): void; destroy(): void; }
  interface YouTubeAPI { Player: new (element: HTMLIFrameElement, options: { events: { onReady: () => void } }) => VideoPlayer; }
  const frame = document.querySelector<HTMLIFrameElement>('#aidan-interview');
  if (frame) {
    const host = window as Window & { YT?: YouTubeAPI; onYouTubeIframeAPIReady?: () => void };
    const motion = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    let player: VideoPlayer | undefined;
    let ready = false;
    let visible = false;
    let disposed = false;
    frame.src += `&origin=${encodeURIComponent(location.origin)}`;
    const sync = () => {
      if (!ready || !player) return;
      if (!visible || document.hidden) player.pauseVideo();
      else if (!motion.matches) { player.mute(); player.playVideo(); }
    };
    const initialise = () => {
      if (disposed || player || !host.YT) return;
      player = new host.YT.Player(frame, { events: { onReady: () => { ready = true; sync(); } } });
    };
    const previousReady = host.onYouTubeIframeAPIReady;
    const apiReady = () => { previousReady?.(); initialise(); };
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
      visible = entries[0].isIntersecting && entries[0].intersectionRatio >= .3;
      if (visible && !player) {
        if (host.YT?.Player) initialise();
        else {
          host.onYouTubeIframeAPIReady = apiReady;
          if (!document.querySelector('script[src="https://www.youtube.com/iframe_api"]')) {
            const script = document.createElement('script');
            script.src = 'https://www.youtube.com/iframe_api';
            document.head.append(script);
          }
        }
      }
      sync();
    }, { threshold: [0, .3] });
    observer.observe(frame);
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', sync);
    motion.addEventListener('change', sync);
    document.addEventListener('astro:before-swap', () => {
      disposed = true;
      observer.disconnect();
      document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', sync);
      motion.removeEventListener('change', sync);
      if (host.onYouTubeIframeAPIReady === apiReady) host.onYouTubeIframeAPIReady = previousReady;
      player?.destroy();
    }, { once: true });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .strategy-hero { padding-top: clamp(120px,18vh,180px); padding-bottom: clamp(48px,7vw,96px); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(38px,5.5vw,82px); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.04em; max-width: 22ch; }
  .strategy-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 28px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 20px; font: 11px var(--font-mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; line-height: 1.6; }
  .strategy-meta span:first-child { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .comparison { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  .hero-comparison,.wide { margin-top: 48px; }
  .comparison-slot { aspect-ratio: 16/10; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: clamp(20px,3vw,48px); display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; }
  .comparison-title { font-size: clamp(22px,3vw,42px); letter-spacing: -.025em; line-height: 1.15; max-width: 14ch; }
  .comparison-note { font: 12px var(--font-mono); color: var(--color-body); }
  :global(.article-section--dark) .comparison-slot { border-color: var(--color-dark-border); }
  :global(.article-section--dark) .comparison-note,:global(.article-section--dark) figcaption { color: var(--color-dark-body); }
  figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  figure.wide { margin-top: 48px; }
  img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
  figcaption { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; max-width: 72ch; color: var(--color-body); }
  figcaption a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .phone { max-width: 360px; padding-top: 18px; }
  .video-frame { aspect-ratio: 16/9; background: #080807; }
  iframe { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; }
  .statement { font-size: clamp(30px,4vw,60px); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -.035em; max-width: 22ch; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .contrast { border-block: 1px solid var(--color-dark-border); padding-block: 24px; }
  .contrast p { font-size: clamp(24px,3vw,42px); line-height: 1.35; }
  .contrast p:first-child { color: var(--color-dark-body); }
  .contrast p:last-child { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .strategy-story :global(.editorial-seq) { margin-top: 0; }
  @media(max-width:600px) { .comparison { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .comparison-slot { aspect-ratio: 16/9; } }
</style>
